      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The vernacular in Post 1 doesn't change the underlying message; the sentiment of replacement and fear is what matters, regardless of the dialect used. Post 2 is \"coded\" because it uses vague, high-minded language to mask a clear exclusionary agenda, whereas Post 4 is more direct in its exclusionary demand for \"people who actually share our values.\" Both are rooted in the same bigoted ideology, but one is more subtle than the other.",
